('source.welsh.mabinogion_guest.gutenberg','The Mabinogion, tr. Lady Charlotte Guest (1838–1849)','Pedair Cainc y Mabinogi','HISTORICAL_TRANSLATION',3,'Project Gutenberg (eBook #5160)','Anonymous (Middle Welsh); translated by Lady Charlotte Guest','lang.en','1849','2026-10-24','https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/5160',NULL,'Pwyll Prince of Dyved; Branwen the Daughter of Llyr; Manawyddan the Son of Llyr; Math the Son of Mathonwy','Public-domain translation distributed by Project Gutenberg','Nineteenth-century English translation of Middle Welsh prose tales preserved in the Red Book of Hergest',NULL,'Public web page',0,'Cite the branch and episode; publish independent retellings rather than the translation.',0,'English translation of the Middle Welsh','URL_SYNTAX_VALID','Project Gutenberg eBook #5160 matched through public search-index metadata on 2026-10-24. Guest''s spellings (Dyved, Annwvyn, Manawyddan) differ from modern Welsh.');

