('hero.greek.danae','Danaë','达那厄','Δανάη','Danaë','HERO','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','Daughter of King Acrisius of Argos, shut in a bronze chamber and visited by Zeus as a shower of gold; mother of Perseus.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.greek.acrisius','Acrisius','阿克里西俄斯','Ἀκρίσιος','Acrisius','HERO','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','King of Argos, warned by an oracle that his daughter''s son would kill him; killed by Perseus''s discus at Larissa.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('person.greek.polydectes','Polydectes','波吕得克忒斯','Πολυδέκτης','Polydectes','PERSON','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth','King of Seriphos who sends Perseus for the Gorgon''s head and is turned to stone by it (Library 2.4.2–2.4.3).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('creature.greek.medusa','Medusa','美杜莎','Μέδουσα','Medusa','MONSTER','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','The only mortal one of the three Gorgons, whose gaze turned onlookers to stone; beheaded by Perseus (Library 2.4.2).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('creature.greek.graeae','Graeae (Phorcides)','格赖埃三姐妹','Γραῖαι','Graeae (Phorcides)','MONSTER','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','The three grey sisters, old from birth, who share one eye and one tooth; Perseus takes them to learn the way to the nymphs (Library 2.4.2).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('creature.greek.pegasus','Pegasus','珀伽索斯','Πήγασος','Pegasus','DIVINE_BEAST','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','Winged horse that sprang from the neck of Medusa when Perseus beheaded her (Library 2.4.2).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.greek.heracles','Heracles','赫拉克勒斯','Ἡρακλῆς','Heracles','HERO','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','Son of Zeus and Alcmena, the greatest of Greek heroes, who performed the twelve labours for Eurystheus and after death on Mount Oeta was received among the gods (Library 2.4.8–2.7.7).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.greek.alcmena','Alcmena','阿尔克墨涅','Ἀλκμήνη','Alcmena','HERO','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','Granddaughter of Perseus and mother of Heracles by Zeus and of Iphicles by Amphitryon (Library 2.4.6–2.4.8).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.greek.amphitryon','Amphitryon','安菲特律翁','Ἀμφιτρύων','Amphitryon','HERO','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','Grandson of Perseus, husband of Alcmena and foster-father of Heracles, exiled from Tiryns to Thebes (Library 2.4.6–2.4.11).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.greek.eurystheus','Eurystheus','欧律斯透斯','Εὐρυσθεύς','Eurystheus','HERO','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','King of Tiryns and Mycenae, born before Heracles through Hera''s contrivance, who imposed the twelve labours (Library 2.4.5, 2.4.12–2.5.12).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.greek.iolaus','Iolaus','伊俄拉俄斯','Ἰόλαος','Iolaus','HERO','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','Son of Iphicles and nephew of Heracles, his charioteer against the Lernaean hydra (Library 2.5.2).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('creature.greek.nemean_lion','Nemean lion','涅墨亚狮子','Νεμέος λέων','Nemean lion','MONSTER','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','Invulnerable lion of Nemea, offspring of Typhon, strangled by Heracles as his first labour (Library 2.5.1).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('creature.greek.lernaean_hydra','Lernaean hydra','勒耳那的许德拉','Λερναία ὕδρα','Lernaean hydra','MONSTER','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','Nine-headed water serpent of the swamp of Lerna whose middle head was immortal; killed by Heracles with Iolaus''s help (Library 2.5.2).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('creature.greek.geryon','Geryon','革律翁','Γηρυών','Geryon','GIANT','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','Triple-bodied giant of the island Erytheia whose red cattle Heracles drove off as his tenth labour (Library 2.5.10).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('creature.greek.cerberus','Cerberus','刻耳柏洛斯','Κέρβερος','Cerberus','MONSTER','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','Three-headed hound of Hades with a serpent''s tail, brought up from the underworld by Heracles as his last labour (Library 2.5.12).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('deity.greek.atlas','Atlas','阿特拉斯','Ἄτλας','Atlas','DEITY','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','Titan who holds up the sky near the Hesperides; he fetches their golden apples for Heracles and is tricked into taking back the sky (Library 2.5.11).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.greek.hippolyte','Hippolyte','希波吕忒','Ἱππολύτη','Hippolyte','HERO','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','Queen of the Amazons whose belt, given by Ares, Heracles fetched for Eurystheus''s daughter (Library 2.5.9).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.greek.deianira','Deianira','得伊阿尼拉','Δηιάνειρα','Deianira','HERO','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','Daughter of Oeneus of Calydon and wife of Heracles, won by his wrestling with Achelous; she unknowingly kills him with the robe smeared with Nessus''s blood (Library 2.7.5–2.7.7).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.greek.iole','Iole','伊俄勒','Ἰόλη','Iole','HERO','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','Daughter of Eurytus of Oechalia, promised as an archery prize and refused to Heracles, later taken captive by him (Library 2.6.1, 2.7.7).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.greek.omphale','Omphale','翁法勒','Ὀμφάλη','Omphale','HERO','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','Queen of Lydia, daughter of Iardanes, who bought Heracles as a slave when Hermes sold him in penance for the murder of Iphitus (Library 2.6.3).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('creature.greek.nessus','Nessus','涅索斯','Νέσσος','Nessus','CREATURE','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','Centaur ferryman of the river Evenus, shot by Heracles for assaulting Deianira; his blood becomes the poison of Heracles''s robe (Library 2.7.6–2.7.7).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('deity.greek.hebe','Hebe','赫柏','Ἥβη','Hebe','DEITY','civ.greek','Greek heroic myth (Library, 1st–2nd century CE compilation)','Goddess of youth, daughter of Zeus and Hera, given in marriage to Heracles after his apotheosis (Library 2.7.7).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.greek.jason','Jason','伊阿宋','Ἰάσων','Jason','HERO','civ.greek','Argonautica (3rd century BCE)','Son of Aeson and leader of the Argonauts, sent by King Pelias to fetch the golden fleece from Colchis, which he wins with Medea''s help.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.greek.pelias','Pelias','珀利阿斯','Πελίας','Pelias','HERO','civ.greek','Argonautica (3rd century BCE)','King of Iolcus, warned to beware the man with one sandal, who sends Jason on the quest for the golden fleece.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.greek.orpheus','Orpheus','俄耳甫斯','Ὀρφεύς','Orpheus','HERO','civ.greek','Argonautica (3rd century BCE)','Thracian singer among the Argonauts, whose song calms quarrels and drowns out the Sirens (Argonautica 1, 4).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.greek.polydeuces','Polydeuces','波吕丢刻斯','Πολυδεύκης','Polydeuces','HERO','civ.greek','Argonautica (3rd century BCE)','Son of Zeus and twin of Castor, the boxer among the Argonauts, who kills the Bebrycian king Amycus (Argonautica 2).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.greek.hylas','Hylas','许拉斯','Ὕλας','Hylas','HERO','civ.greek','Argonautica (3rd century BCE)','Young companion of Heracles, drawn into a spring by a water-nymph in Mysia, so that Heracles is left behind (Argonautica 1).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.greek.phineus','Phineus','菲纽斯（盲眼先知）','Φινεύς','Phineus','HERO','civ.greek','Argonautica (3rd century BCE)','Blind seer of Thrace tormented by the Harpies, freed by the sons of Boreas, who foretells the Argonauts'' route (Argonautica 2).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.greek.hypsipyle','Hypsipyle','许普西皮勒','Ὑψιπύλη','Hypsipyle','HERO','civ.greek','Argonautica (3rd century BCE)','Queen of Lemnos, whose women had killed their menfolk, who welcomes Jason and the Argonauts (Argonautica 1).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.greek.apsyrtus','Apsyrtus','阿布绪耳托斯','Ἄψυρτος','Apsyrtus','HERO','civ.greek','Argonautica (3rd century BCE)','Son of Aeetes and brother of Medea, who pursues the Argonauts and is killed by Jason in an ambush (Argonautica 4).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('deity.greek.eros','Eros','厄洛斯','Ἔρως','Eros','DEITY','civ.greek','Argonautica (3rd century BCE)','Child of Aphrodite whose arrow, shot at Hera''s request, makes Medea fall in love with Jason (Argonautica 3).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('creature.greek.harpies','Harpies','哈耳庇厄','Ἅρπυιαι','Harpies','MONSTER','civ.greek','Argonautica (3rd century BCE)','Winged snatchers who befoul and steal the food of the blind seer Phineus until the sons of Boreas drive them away (Argonautica 2).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('creature.greek.talos','Talos','塔罗斯','Τάλως','Talos','GIANT','civ.greek','Argonautica (3rd century BCE)','Bronze giant who guards Crete by hurling rocks at ships, destroyed by Medea''s spells through the vein at his ankle (Argonautica 4).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('artifact.greek.argo','Argo','阿尔戈号','Ἀργώ','Argo','SHIP','civ.greek','Argonautica (3rd century BCE)','The ship of the Argonauts, built by Argus under Athena''s direction, with a speaking beam of Dodonian oak (Argonautica 1, 4).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('artifact.greek.golden_fleece','Golden fleece','金羊毛','χρύσειον κῶας','chryseion kōas','SACRED_OBJECT','civ.greek','Argonautica (3rd century BCE)','Fleece of the golden ram that carried Phrixus to Colchis, hung in the grove of Ares and guarded by a sleepless serpent (Argonautica 2, 4).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('deity.norse.vidar','Víðarr','维达','Víðarr','Víðarr','DEITY','civ.norse','Old Norse literature (13th century)','Silent son of Odin who avenges his father at Ragnarök by tearing Fenrir''s jaws apart, and survives into the renewed world (Gylfaginning 51, 53).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('creature.norse.surtr','Surtr','苏尔特','Surtr','Surtr','GIANT','civ.norse','Old Norse literature (13th century)','Fire giant of Muspell who leads its sons at Ragnarök, kills Freyr and burns the whole world (Gylfaginning 4, 51).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('creature.norse.garm','Garmr','加姆','Garmr','Garmr','MONSTER','civ.norse','Old Norse literature (13th century)','Hound bound before Gnipahellir who breaks loose at Ragnarök and fights Týr, each killing the other (Gylfaginning 51).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('artifact.norse.naglfar','Naglfar','纳吉尔法','Naglfar','Naglfar','SHIP','civ.norse','Old Norse literature (13th century)','Ship made of dead men''s nails that is loosed at Ragnarök and steered by the giant Hrymr (Gylfaginning 51).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.norse.volsung','Völsungr','沃尔松格','Völsungr','Völsungr','HERO','civ.norse','Old Norse literature (13th century)','King of Hunland, great-grandson of Odin, born after six years in the womb, who built his hall round the oak Branstock and fell fighting Siggeir (Völsunga saga 2–5).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.norse.signy','Signý','西格妮','Signý','Signý','HERO','civ.norse','Old Norse literature (13th century)','Daughter of Völsungr and twin of Sigmundr, married against her will to Siggeir, who bears Sinfjötli to her brother and dies in Siggeir''s burning hall (Völsunga saga 3–8).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.norse.sigmund','Sigmundr','西格蒙德','Sigmundr','Sigmundr','HERO','civ.norse','Old Norse literature (13th century)','Son of Völsungr who alone draws Odin''s sword from the Branstock, avenges his father, and dies when Odin breaks his sword; father of Sigurðr (Völsunga saga 3–12).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.norse.sinfjotli','Sinfjötli','辛菲奥特利','Sinfjötli','Sinfjötli','HERO','civ.norse','Old Norse literature (13th century)','Son of Sigmundr and his sister Signý, raised in the forest to avenge the Völsungs, poisoned by Borghildr and carried off by a mysterious ferryman (Völsunga saga 7–10).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.norse.sigurd','Sigurðr','西古尔德','Sigurðr','Sigurðr','HERO','civ.norse','Old Norse literature (13th century)','Son of Sigmundr and Hjördís, slayer of the dragon Fáfnir, who wakes Brynhildr and is killed through the Gjúkungs'' oath-breaking (Völsunga saga 13–32).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('being.norse.regin','Reginn','雷金','Reginn','Reginn','DWARF','civ.norse','Old Norse literature (13th century)','Dwarf-like smith, son of Hreiðmarr and brother of Fáfnir, who fosters Sigurðr, reforges Gram and plots to betray him after the dragon is slain (Völsunga saga 13–19).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('creature.norse.fafnir','Fáfnir','法夫纳','Fáfnir','Fáfnir','DRAGON','civ.norse','Old Norse literature (13th century)','Son of Hreiðmarr who killed his father for the otter-ransom gold and became a dragon lying on it at Gnitaheiðr, slain by Sigurðr (Völsunga saga 14, 18).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('being.norse.andvari','Andvari','安德瓦利','Andvari','Andvari','DWARF','civ.norse','Old Norse literature (13th century)','Dwarf who lived as a pike in a waterfall and was forced by Loki to give up his gold and ring, laying a curse on both (Völsunga saga 14).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.norse.brynhild','Brynhildr','布伦希尔德','Brynhildr','Brynhildr','HERO','civ.norse','Old Norse literature (13th century)','Shield-maiden put to sleep by Odin''s sleep-thorn for disobeying him, woken by Sigurðr, betrothed to him, and later deceived into marrying Gunnarr (Völsunga saga 20–32).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('artifact.norse.andvaranaut','Andvaranautr','安德瓦拉诺特','Andvaranautr','Andvaranaut','RING','civ.norse','Old Norse literature (13th century)','Ring of the dwarf Andvari, cursed by him to bring death to its owners; taken by Loki, passed through Fáfnir to Sigurðr and Brynhildr (Völsunga saga 14, 24, 27–28).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('creature.norse.grani','Grani','格拉尼','Grani','Grani','DIVINE_BEAST','civ.norse','Old Norse literature (13th century)','Grey horse of the kin of Sleipnir, chosen by Sigurðr with Odin''s advice, who carries the dragon''s hoard (Völsunga saga 13, 19).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.norse.gudrun','Guðrún','古德伦','Guðrún','Guðrún','HERO','civ.norse','Old Norse literature (13th century)','Daughter of King Gjúki, married to Sigurðr after her mother''s potion makes him forget Brynhildr; her quarrel with Brynhildr leads to his death (Völsunga saga 25–31).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.norse.gunnar','Gunnarr','贡纳尔','Gunnarr','Gunnarr','HERO','civ.norse','Old Norse literature (13th century)','Son of Gjúki, who wins Brynhildr through Sigurðr riding the flames in his shape and later consents to Sigurðr''s killing (Völsunga saga 26–32).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.irish.medb','Medb','梅芙','Medb','Medb','HERO','civ.irish','Ulster Cycle (Book of Leinster, 12th century)','Queen of Connacht who musters the four provinces to carry off the Brown Bull of Cúailnge so that her wealth will equal her husband''s (Táin Bó Cúalnge).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.irish.ailill','Ailill mac Máta','艾利尔','Ailill mac Máta','Ailill mac Máta','HERO','civ.irish','Ulster Cycle (Book of Leinster, 12th century)','King of Connacht and husband of Medb, whose bull Finnbennach makes his possessions greater than hers (Táin Bó Cúalnge).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.irish.ferdiad','Fer Diad','费迪亚德','Fer Diad','Fer Diad','HERO','civ.irish','Ulster Cycle (Book of Leinster, 12th century)','Foster-brother of Cú Chulainn, trained with him by Scáthach, who is persuaded by Medb to fight him at the ford and is killed on the fourth day (Táin Bó Cúalnge).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.irish.conchobar','Conchobar mac Nessa','康胡巴尔','Conchobar mac Nessa','Conchobar mac Nessa','HERO','civ.irish','Ulster Cycle (Book of Leinster, 12th century)','King of Ulster at Emain Macha, uncle and foster-father of Cú Chulainn, who leads the Ulstermen when they rise from their debility (Táin Bó Cúalnge).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('creature.irish.donn_cuailnge','Donn Cúailnge','库利的褐色公牛','Donn Cúailnge','Donn Cúailnge','DIVINE_BEAST','civ.irish','Ulster Cycle (Book of Leinster, 12th century)','The Brown Bull of Cúailnge, whose seizure by Medb is the object of the Táin; it kills Finnbennach and dies of its own exertions (Táin Bó Cúalnge).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('creature.irish.finnbennach','Finnbennach','白角公牛','Findbennach Aí','Finnbennach','DIVINE_BEAST','civ.irish','Ulster Cycle (Book of Leinster, 12th century)','The White-horned Bull of Connacht, born in Medb''s herd but unwilling to be owned by a woman, who goes over to Ailill''s herd and is killed by the Brown Bull (Táin Bó Cúalnge).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.welsh.pwyll','Pwyll','皮威尔','Pwyll Pendefig Dyfed','Pwyll','HERO','civ.welsh','Four Branches of the Mabinogi (Middle Welsh, c. 11th–12th century)','Prince of Dyfed who changes places with Arawn, king of Annwn, for a year, wins Rhiannon and is called Head of Annwn (First Branch).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.welsh.rhiannon','Rhiannon','里安农','Rhiannon','Rhiannon','HERO','civ.welsh','Four Branches of the Mabinogi (Middle Welsh, c. 11th–12th century)','Lady of the Otherworld on a white horse who chooses Pwyll, is falsely accused of killing her son, and later marries Manawydan (First and Third Branches).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.welsh.pryderi','Pryderi','普雷德里','Pryderi','Pryderi','HERO','civ.welsh','Four Branches of the Mabinogi (Middle Welsh, c. 11th–12th century)','Son of Pwyll and Rhiannon, stolen at birth and raised by Teyrnon as Gwri Golden-hair, later lord of Dyfed, killed by Gwydion (First to Fourth Branches).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('deity.welsh.arawn','Arawn','阿拉文','Arawn','Arawn','DEITY','civ.welsh','Four Branches of the Mabinogi (Middle Welsh, c. 11th–12th century)','King of Annwn, the Otherworld, who exchanges shapes and kingdoms with Pwyll for a year so that Pwyll may defeat his rival Hafgan (First Branch).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('place.welsh.annwn','Annwn','安农（彼世）','Annwn','Annwn','REALM','civ.welsh','Four Branches of the Mabinogi (Middle Welsh, c. 11th–12th century)','The Welsh Otherworld ruled by Arawn, a realm of feasting and splendour where Pwyll spends a year (First Branch).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.welsh.bendigeidfran','Bendigeidfran','本迪盖德弗兰（受福的布兰）','Bendigeidfran fab Llŷr','Bendigeidfran','HERO','civ.welsh','Four Branches of the Mabinogi (Middle Welsh, c. 11th–12th century)','Giant king of the Island of the Mighty, son of Llŷr, who wades to Ireland to avenge his sister Branwen and whose severed head presides over the feast at Harlech and Gwales (Second Branch).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.welsh.branwen','Branwen','布兰雯','Branwen ferch Llŷr','Branwen','HERO','civ.welsh','Four Branches of the Mabinogi (Middle Welsh, c. 11th–12th century)','Daughter of Llŷr, married to Matholwch of Ireland and humiliated there, who sends a starling to her brother and dies of grief that two islands were laid waste for her (Second Branch).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.welsh.manawydan','Manawydan','马纳维丹','Manawydan fab Llŷr','Manawydan','HERO','civ.welsh','Four Branches of the Mabinogi (Middle Welsh, c. 11th–12th century)','Son of Llŷr, brother of Bendigeidfran, one of the seven survivors of the war in Ireland, who marries Rhiannon and lifts the enchantment on Dyfed (Second and Third Branches).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.welsh.matholwch','Matholwch','马索卢赫','Matholwch','Matholwch','HERO','civ.welsh','Four Branches of the Mabinogi (Middle Welsh, c. 11th–12th century)','King of Ireland who marries Branwen and, insulted by Efnysien''s maiming of his horses, receives the cauldron of rebirth in amends (Second Branch).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.welsh.efnysien','Efnysien','埃夫尼辛','Efnysien','Efnysien','HERO','civ.welsh','Four Branches of the Mabinogi (Middle Welsh, c. 11th–12th century)','Quarrelsome half-brother of Bendigeidfran who maims Matholwch''s horses, throws Gwern into the fire and breaks the cauldron of rebirth at the cost of his life (Second Branch).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('artifact.welsh.cauldron_of_rebirth','Cauldron of rebirth','复生之釜','Pair Dadeni','Pair Dadeni','SACRED_OBJECT','civ.welsh','Four Branches of the Mabinogi (Middle Welsh)','Cauldron from Ireland that restores the slain to life though without speech, given by Bendigeidfran to Matholwch and broken by Efnysien (Second Branch).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.welsh.math','Math fab Mathonwy','马斯','Math fab Mathonwy','Math fab Mathonwy','HERO','civ.welsh','Four Branches of the Mabinogi (Middle Welsh, c. 11th–12th century)','Magician-king of Gwynedd who must keep his feet in a maiden''s lap except in war, punishes his nephews by turning them into beasts, and with Gwydion makes Blodeuedd from flowers (Fourth Branch).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.welsh.gwydion','Gwydion','格威迪恩','Gwydion fab Dôn','Gwydion','HERO','civ.welsh','Four Branches of the Mabinogi (Middle Welsh, c. 11th–12th century)','Magician and storyteller, nephew of Math, who tricks Pryderi out of his swine, raises Lleu, outwits Arianrhod''s curses and turns Blodeuedd into an owl (Fourth Branch).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.welsh.arianrhod','Arianrhod','阿丽安萝德','Arianrhod ferch Dôn','Arianrhod','HERO','civ.welsh','Four Branches of the Mabinogi (Middle Welsh, c. 11th–12th century)','Daughter of Dôn who fails Math''s test of maidenhood, bearing Dylan and Lleu, and lays three destinies on Lleu: no name, no arms and no human wife save from her (Fourth Branch).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.welsh.lleu','Lleu Llaw Gyffes','勒伊·劳·吉菲斯','Lleu Llaw Gyffes','Lleu Llaw Gyffes','HERO','civ.welsh','Four Branches of the Mabinogi (Middle Welsh, c. 11th–12th century)','Son of Arianrhod, named ''the fair one with the skilful hand'', armed and married through Gwydion''s craft, who survives Blodeuedd''s betrayal as an eagle (Fourth Branch).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('hero.welsh.blodeuedd','Blodeuedd','布罗黛维德','Blodeuedd','Blodeuedd','HERO','civ.welsh','Four Branches of the Mabinogi (Middle Welsh, c. 11th–12th century)','Woman made by Math and Gwydion from the flowers of oak, broom and meadowsweet as Lleu''s wife, who plots his death with Gronw Pebr and is turned into an owl (Fourth Branch).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('text.norse.volsunga_saga','Völsunga saga','沃尔松格萨迦','Völsunga saga','Völsunga saga','TEXT','civ.norse','13th century (Iceland)','Thirteenth-century Icelandic prose saga of the Völsung family, from Sigi son of Odin to Sigurðr, Brynhildr and Guðrún, retelling heroic poems of the Poetic Edda.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('text.irish.tain_bo_cuailnge','Táin Bó Cúailnge','夺牛长征记','Táin Bó Cúailnge','Táin Bó Cúailnge','TEXT','civ.irish','Old and Middle Irish recensions (11th–12th century manuscripts)','Central epic of the Ulster Cycle, in which Medb of Connacht invades Ulster for the Brown Bull of Cúailnge and Cú Chulainn defends the fords alone.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z'),
('text.welsh.four_branches','Four Branches of the Mabinogi','马比诺吉昂四支','Pedair Cainc y Mabinogi','Pedair Cainc y Mabinogi','TEXT','civ.welsh','Middle Welsh (composition c. 11th–12th century)','Four linked Middle Welsh prose tales — Pwyll, Branwen, Manawydan and Math — in which Pryderi appears in each branch.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z','2026-10-24T12:00:00Z');

